===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|h₁én}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*gew-|*weyp-|*-Hō}}
The {{glossary|adverb}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|enviroun|t=round about in a circle or ring; all around}}{{nb...|enuyroun, enveroun, environ, enviroun, enviroune, envroun, envyron, envyroun, envyrowne, inviroun, in viroun, invirown, invirowne, invyroun, invyrown|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=envīrǒun|pos=adv|id=MED14189}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|enviroun}}, {{m|xno|environ}}{{nb...|enveron, envirun|otherforms=1}}, and {{der|en|frm|enviroun}}, {{m|frm|environ}}{{nb...|envirun|otherforms=1}}, from {{der|en|fro|environ|t=around, surrounding; about, approximately, roughly}} (modern {{cog|fr|environ}}), from {{m|fro|en-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘in; into’}} + {{m|fro|viron|t=circuit; circumference, compass; country round about}} (though first attested later)<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|entry=† environ|pos=adv.'' and ''prep|id=63081|date=December 2021}}</ref> (from {{m|fro|virer|t=to bear, turn, veer}} (either from {{der|en|la|gȳrō|t=to turn in a circle, rotate; to circle, revolve around}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gew-|t=to bend, curve; an arch, vault}}), or from {{der|en|la|vibrō|t=to hurl, launch; shake; to tremble, vibrate}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*weyp-|*weyb-, *weyp-|to shake; to tremble; to sway, swing; to rotate, turn, wind, wrap (around)}})) + {{m|fro|-on|pos={{glossary|augmentative}} {{glossary|suffix}}}}).

The {{glossary|preposition}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|enviroun|t=around the outside or perimeter of; all around; about or throughout the extent of}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=envīrǒun|pos=prep|id=MED14190}}</ref> which is from the adverb.<ref name="OED"/>

