#* {{quote-book|en|author=John Denton|chapter=Burgh Barony|editor=[[w:Richard Saul Ferguson|R[ichard] S[aul] Ferguson]]|title=An Accompt of the Most Considerable Estates and Families in the County of Cumberland, from the Conquest unto the Beginning of the Reign of K. [[w:James VI and I|James [the First]]]|location=Kendal, Cumbria|publisher=T. Wilson|month=(date written)|year=c. 1610|year_published=1887|page=76|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=a_8UAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA76|oclc=15617822|passage=There is another village called Finland, Fingland and Fennland, which is almost '''environned''' with a moss and fenny ground.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Poems 1673|sonnet=XII|page=56|passage=I did but prompt the age to quit their cloggs / By the knovvn rules of antient libertie, / When ſtrait a barbarous noiſe '''environs''' me / Of Ovvles and Cuckoes, Aſſes, Apes and Doggs.}}
#* {{RQ:Cowper Task|page=12|passage=[W]ent I forth, and found, till then unknovvn, / A cottage, vvhither oft vve ſince repair: / 'Tis perch'd upon the green-hill top, but cloſe / '''Inviron'd''' vvith a ring of branching elms / That overhang the thatch, itſelf unſeen, / Peeps at the vale belovv; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Theodore Parker|chapter=[Prayer] XXX|title=Prayers|location=Boston, Mass.|publisher=Walker, Wise, and Company|date=23 May 1858|year_published=1862|page=148|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=_LU-XPsjexQC&pg=PA148|oclc=5665856|passage=We bless thee for the material world, wherewith thou '''environest''' us beneath and about and overhead.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Haunted House|chapter=The Mortals in the House|page=1|column=1|passage=Under none of the accredited ghostly circumstances, and '''environed''' by none of the conventional ghostly surroundings, did I first make acquaintance with the house which is the subject of this Christmas piece.}}
