##* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:John Woody Papworth|John W[oody] Papworth]]|entry=1 ANNULET betw. or within&nbsp;… and in chief&nbsp;…|editor=Alfred W. Morant|title=An Alphabetical Dictionary of Coats of Arms Belonging to Families in Great Britain and Ireland;{{nb...|Forming an Extensive Ordinary of British Armorials; upon an Entirely New Plan, in which the Arms are Systematically Subdivided throughout, and so Arranged in Alphabetical Order that the Names of Families whose Shields are Found on Buildings, Monuments, Seals, Paintings, Plate, etc., whether Mediæval or Modern, can be Readily Ascertained.}}|location=London|publisher=T. Richards,{{nb...|37, Great Queen Street.}}|year=1874|page=4|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=rjEGAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA4|column=2|oclc=460013398|passage=Az[ure], an annulet '''environing''' a barrulet, betw[een] two bars and in chief a cross patty fitchy or.}}
