#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joshua Stopford|chapter=Altars|title=Pagano-papismus: Or, An Exact Parallel Between Rome-pagan, and Rome-Christian, in Their Doctrines and Ceremonies|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed by}} A. Maxwell, for R. Clavel,{{nb...|at the sign of the Peacock in St. Pauls Church-Yard.}}|year=1675|page=75|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=N0KMVOE8Yx0C&pg=PA75|oclc=65623403|passage=O moſt high God, who keepeſt all things whether high or low, and '''environeſt''' every creature; ſancti†fie and bleſs† theſe Creatures of lime and ſand; Through Chriſt our Lord, Amen.|footer={{small|The † symbol indicates the point at which the bishop makes the sign of the cross.}}}}
#* {{RQ:Hume History|volume=4|chapter=III|page=543|passage=[T]he admiral in particular, being dangerouſly vvounded, and '''environed''' by the guards of the King, on vvhose protection he ſeemed entirely to rely, had no means of eſcape, and might ſurely, before his death, have been convicted of the crimes imputed to him: {{...}}}}
