===Etymology 3===
From Late {{inh|en|enm|invyroun}}, {{inh|en|enm|enuyroun}}, {{m|enm|enuyrown}}, from {{der|en|xno|enviroun}}, {{m|xno|environ}}, {{m|xno|envirun}}, and {{der|en|frm|environ|t=circumference; surroundings; (''in the plural'') boundaries, frontiers}} {{qualifier|chiefly in the plural}} (modern {{cog|fr|environ}}), a {{glossary|noun}} use of {{der|en|fro|environ|pos=adverb}}: see [[#Etymology 1|etymology 1]].<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=63079|date=March 2022}}</ref>

